# Memory Gate practice build: configuration contract (no values here, ever).
#
# `npm run env:push` reads keys from auth/memory-gate.env (ignored, mode 600), or $MEMORY_GATE_ENV,
# with $MEMGATE_AUTH_FILE accepted as a compatibility alias. MEMORY_GATE_ENV takes precedence.
# It stores them in the LOCAL Convex deployment's environment. Browser code receives only short-lived room tokens.
# Then it writes `.env.worker` (mode 600, gitignored) for local tools. Never commit populated credentials files.
#
# --- provider keys (in auth/memory-gate.env) ---
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=        required for live Claude (flag ai.live); without it the deterministic mock runs ("mock" badge)
# ANTHROPIC_WORKSPACE_ID=   required with an org-level key (sent as the anthropic-workspace-id header)
# CARTESIA_API_KEY=         required for live speech (flags stt.live, tts.live); without it: typed input + captions only
# TRIPO_API_KEY=            optional: personalize/generate objects (flag objects.live); the library works without it
# WORLD_LABS_API_KEY=       optional: private Marble 1.1 ordinary-photo worlds, normally 1,580 API credits each (flag worldlabs.generate; one active, three total per room)
# WORLD_LABS_GENERATION_LIMIT=3  deployment-wide lifetime submission cap; survives room deletion. Raise deliberately for a later funded run, never automatically.
# MODAL_TOKEN_ID=           optional: the GPU worker (SHARP on Modal L40S); without it new photos use the sample room
# MODAL_TOKEN_SECRET=       optional: as above (the Modal account needs a payment method for any GPU)
#
# --- generated by `npm run env:push` into .env.worker (and the Convex env) ---
# WORKER_SECRET=            guards the worker/seed endpoints (convex/splats.ts, convex/admin.ts)
# ADMIN_CODE=               the operator code for deployment-wide live-service flags (phone admin screen)
# CONVEX_URL=               the local backend, http://127.0.0.1:3210 (copied from .env.local, written by `convex dev`)

# --- new exchange: put these in ignored .env.exchange, not frontend environment ---
# SPACETIME_BIN=spacetime   installed SpacetimeDB 2.13.0 CLI executable (absolute path supported)
# SPACETIME_URL=ws://127.0.0.1:3000
# SPACETIME_DATABASE=heirloom-exchange
# SPACETIME_TOKEN=          publishing identity; automatically read from project .spacetime/config/cli.toml locally
# ATLAS_MODE=local          actual Apify SDK Actor, public archive requests, no cloud token needed
# EXCHANGE_ORIGINS=         exact comma-separated phone and gate origins (5173/5174 phone, 5180/4180 gate); local:up derives this machine's LAN origins
# For an explicitly enabled Apify cloud Actor (unverified until a real cloud run):
# ATLAS_MODE=cloud
# ALLOW_APIFY_CLOUD=1
# APIFY_TOKEN=              server only; do not paste into the browser or Git
# APIFY_ACTOR_ID=           your published actor ID or username~actor-name
